00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:00.000
I said, this could get good, because, you know,

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:30.000
That's not the best place to be in the whole world, and everything I told you earlier about how important that race is to me is just the same for everybody. I knew he wasn't going to let out just to run second. He was going for it, and they got together, and I got in the lead, and then I just kept thinking, please don't have a caution. As soon as I got by them on the back straightaway, I looked in my mirror to see if they were wrecking or what happened, and when they weren't wrecking and Rusty cleared them or was right there clearing them, I knew they were wrecking.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.000
I knew I had to outrun one of the toughest guys in the business for basically nine laps.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.000
Just because I got the lead didn't mean I thought I had it won.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.000
So it wasn't any time for excitement.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:44.000
It was just time to settle down there and try to run the best nine laps I've ever run in my whole life.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.000
And that's what I did.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.000
And I just was fortunate in the fact that my car worked.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.000
I mean, it did just what I wanted it to do.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:54.000
I could smoke down in the corner, didn't turn, and I would go.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:58.000
So once I ran a couple of laps like that, I knew they weren't going to catch me.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.990
I just kind of started thinking as long as they don't

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:03.250
